a:2:{s:7:"content";s:2355:"<p>It is a group of metabolic diseases characterized by increased levels of glucose in the blood ( hyperglycemia ), resulting from defects in either or both of the following:</p>
<p><strong>1) Insulin production:</strong> Pancreatic Beta cells may stop secreting insulin i.e (Type-1 Diabetes Mellitus).</p>
<p><strong>2) Insulin Action:</strong> The body cells may stop responding to insulin or there is insulin resistance e (Type-2 Diabetes Mellitus)</p>
<h2>Types Of Diabetes Mellitus</h2>
<p><strong>Type-1</strong></p>
<p>In diabetes type 1, the pancreas does not make insulin, because the body's immune system attacks the islet cells in the pancreas that make insulin.</p>
<ul>
<li>Genetic Predisposition – HLA genes</li>
<li>Autoimmune disease against Beta cells in the pancreas. Possibly viral, which causes destruction of Beta cells ( Decreased Insulin Production )</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Type-2</strong></p>
<p>Insulin ( high, normal or low) present but can not be utilized by body cells i.e ( Insulin resistance ) &gt;&gt; Other specific types ( Secondary)</p>
<ul>
<li>Gestational Diabetes: Typically associated with pregnant women</li>
<li>LADA (Latent autoimmune diabetes in Adults )</li>
</ul>
